        "node_id": "n_8_b62fd7",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (revised): Instead of trying to find the maximum sorted subarray across both halves directly, focus on finding the longest sorted subarray within each half separately and then determine how these subarrays can be combined optimally without violating the rule of removing only one half at a time. This approach ensures that we respect the constraints of the Thanos sort algorithm while maximizing the length of the sorted subarray.",
